1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,102
Welcome to Unit Ten, the last unit of
Algebra One: radicals and data. In this

2
00:00:05,102 --> 00:00:07,488
lesson, we'll simplify square roots.

3
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:13,535
The key rule: the square root of a times b
equals the square root of a, times the

4
00:00:13,535 --> 00:00:14,564
square root of b.

5
00:00:15,014 --> 00:00:19,886
So look for perfect square factors, like
four, nine, sixteen, twenty-five and

6
00:00:19,886 --> 00:00:20,582
thirty-six.

7
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,577
Simplify the square root of fifty.

8
00:00:24,027 --> 00:00:28,960
Fifty is twenty-five times two. So it's
the square root of twenty-five, times the

9
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:31,579
square root of two, which is five root
two.

10
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:37,505
Variables work the same way. The square
root of x squared is x, for x not

11
00:00:37,505 --> 00:00:38,097
negative.

12
00:00:38,547 --> 00:00:44,180
The square root of eighteen x cubed is the
square root of nine x squared times two x,

13
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:46,035
which is three x root two x.

14
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:51,199
To multiply radicals, multiply what's
inside, then simplify.

15
00:00:51,649 --> 00:00:57,089
Root six times root ten is root sixty,
which is root four times fifteen, or two

16
00:00:57,089 --> 00:00:57,985
root fifteen.

17
00:00:59,133 --> 00:01:04,880
A simplified answer has no radical in the
denominator. To fix one, multiply top and

18
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:06,472
bottom by that radical.

19
00:01:06,922 --> 00:01:09,781
Three over root two becomes three root two
over two.

20
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,844
Your turn. Simplify the square root of
seventy-two.

21
00:01:14,294 --> 00:01:15,745
Pause the video and try it.

22
00:01:16,195 --> 00:01:20,333
Seventy-two is thirty-six times two, so
the answer is six root two.

23
00:01:21,466 --> 00:01:25,839
Let's simplify radicals with variables and
rationalize a denominator.

24
00:01:27,266 --> 00:01:33,165
Simplify the square root of seventy two x
to the fifth, assuming x is positive. Then

25
00:01:33,165 --> 00:01:35,202
simplify six over root three.

26
00:01:36,333 --> 00:01:41,538
Find the largest perfect square factor of
seventy two. That's thirty six, times two.

27
00:01:42,666 --> 00:01:46,954
Split x to the fifth into x to the fourth,
a perfect square, times x.

28
00:01:48,099 --> 00:01:52,913
Take out the squares: root thirty six is
six, and root x to the fourth is x

29
00:01:52,913 --> 00:01:55,865
squared. That leaves six x squared root
two x.

30
00:01:56,999 --> 00:02:02,717
For part b, rationalize the denominator by
multiplying top and bottom by root three.

31
00:02:03,866 --> 00:02:08,090
That gives six root three over three,
which simplifies to two root three.

32
00:02:09,233 --> 00:02:13,542
Part a is six x squared root two x, and
part b is two root three.

33
00:02:14,666 --> 00:02:19,905
Watch out. Use the largest perfect square
factor, or you'll have to simplify again.

34
00:02:19,905 --> 00:02:24,575
Even powers come out halved. And a
simplified answer has no radical in the

35
00:02:24,575 --> 00:02:25,333
denominator.

36
00:02:25,466 --> 00:02:31,607
Your turn. Simplify the square root of
fifty y cubed. Pause the video and try it.

37
00:02:36,133 --> 00:02:42,179
Fifty is twenty five times two, and y
cubed is y squared times y. The answer is

38
00:02:42,179 --> 00:02:43,557
five y root two y.

39
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:50,140
Adding radicals works a lot like combining
like terms. In this lesson, we'll see how.

40
00:02:51,267 --> 00:02:53,869
Like radicals have the same number under
the root.

41
00:02:54,319 --> 00:03:00,607
Three root five plus two root five is five
root five, just like three x plus two x is

42
00:03:00,607 --> 00:03:01,125
five x.

43
00:03:02,267 --> 00:03:06,917
Sometimes you need to simplify first. Root
twelve plus root twenty-seven.

44
00:03:07,367 --> 00:03:11,866
Root twelve is two root three, and root
twenty-seven is three root three.

45
00:03:11,866 --> 00:03:13,469
Together, five root three.

46
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:18,781
You can distribute too. Root two times the
quantity three plus root eight.

47
00:03:19,231 --> 00:03:23,434
That's three root two plus root sixteen,
which is three root two plus four.

48
00:03:24,567 --> 00:03:29,371
Radicals appear when you use the
Pythagorean theorem. A right triangle has

49
00:03:29,371 --> 00:03:30,540
legs two and four.

50
00:03:30,990 --> 00:03:36,404
The hypotenuse is the square root of four
plus sixteen, which is root twenty, or two

51
00:03:36,404 --> 00:03:37,049
root five.

52
00:03:38,167 --> 00:03:41,345
Watch out: root two plus root three is not
root five.

53
00:03:41,795 --> 00:03:43,779
You can only combine like radicals.

54
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:47,887
Your turn. Simplify root eighteen plus
root fifty.

55
00:03:48,337 --> 00:03:49,787
Pause the video and try it.

56
00:03:50,237 --> 00:03:55,613
Root eighteen is three root two, and root
fifty is five root two. The total is eight

57
00:03:55,613 --> 00:03:56,189
root two.

58
00:03:57,333 --> 00:04:02,346
Here's a worked example where radicals
only become like terms after simplifying.

59
00:04:03,766 --> 00:04:08,801
Simplify three root twelve minus root
seventy five plus two root twenty seven.

60
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:15,444
Simplify each radical first. Root twelve
is two root three, so three root twelve is

61
00:04:15,444 --> 00:04:16,440
six root three.

62
00:04:17,566 --> 00:04:22,110
Root seventy five is root twenty five
times root three, five root three.

63
00:04:23,233 --> 00:04:28,140
Root twenty seven is three root three, so
two root twenty seven is six root three.

64
00:04:29,266 --> 00:04:32,338
Now all three are like terms, multiples of
root three.

65
00:04:33,466 --> 00:04:38,608
Combine the coefficients: six minus five
plus six is seven. Seven root three.

66
00:04:39,733 --> 00:04:42,442
The expression simplifies to seven root
three.

67
00:04:43,566 --> 00:04:48,868
Watch out. Simplify every radical before
you try to combine. You can only combine

68
00:04:48,868 --> 00:04:54,105
radicals with the same radicand. And root
a plus root b is not root of a plus b.

69
00:04:55,233 --> 00:05:00,388
Your turn. Simplify root eighteen plus
four root two minus root eight. Pause the

70
00:05:00,388 --> 00:05:01,484
video and try it.

71
00:05:06,033 --> 00:05:10,342
Three root two plus four root two minus
two root two is five root two.

72
00:05:11,466 --> 00:05:16,733
Now we turn to statistics. In this lesson,
we'll describe a data set with its center

73
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:17,674
and its spread.

74
00:05:18,799 --> 00:05:22,959
The mean is the average: add the values
and divide by how many there are.

75
00:05:23,409 --> 00:05:28,711
For two, four, four, five and ten, the sum
is twenty-five, and there are five values,

76
00:05:28,711 --> 00:05:29,959
so the mean is five.

77
00:05:31,099 --> 00:05:34,363
The median is the middle value when the
data is in order.

78
00:05:34,813 --> 00:05:39,982
For two, four, four, five, ten, the median
is four. With an even number of values,

79
00:05:39,982 --> 00:05:41,747
average the two middle ones.

80
00:05:42,866 --> 00:05:47,154
The range is the largest minus the
smallest: ten minus two is eight.

81
00:05:47,604 --> 00:05:52,365
The interquartile range, or IQR, is the
spread of the middle half: the third

82
00:05:52,365 --> 00:05:54,495
quartile minus the first quartile.

83
00:05:55,633 --> 00:06:01,461
An outlier is a value far from the rest. A
common rule flags anything more than one

84
00:06:01,461 --> 00:06:04,059
and a half IQRs beyond the quartiles.

85
00:06:04,509 --> 00:06:08,093
Outliers pull the mean toward them, but
barely move the median.

86
00:06:09,233 --> 00:06:13,883
So for skewed data or data with outliers,
use the median and IQR.

87
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:19,448
For symmetric data, the mean and standard
deviation work well. Standard deviation

88
00:06:19,448 --> 00:06:22,227
measures the typical distance from the
mean.

89
00:06:23,366 --> 00:06:27,414
Your turn. Find the mean and median of
three, seven, eight, nine and

90
00:06:27,414 --> 00:06:28,187
twenty-three.

91
00:06:28,637 --> 00:06:30,088
Pause the video and try it.

92
00:06:30,538 --> 00:06:34,817
The sum is fifty, so the mean is ten. The
median is eight. The outlier,

93
00:06:34,817 --> 00:06:36,746
twenty-three, pulls the mean up.

94
00:06:37,866 --> 00:06:41,941
Let's compute center and spread, and see
how an outlier changes them.

95
00:06:43,366 --> 00:06:48,627
Eight students worked these weekly hours:
six, eight, eight, ten, eleven, twelve,

96
00:06:48,627 --> 00:06:53,888
fourteen and forty three. Find the mean,
median and interquartile range. Is forty

97
00:06:53,888 --> 00:06:54,993
three an outlier?

98
00:06:56,133 --> 00:07:00,507
The sum is one hundred twelve, so the mean
is one twelve over eight, which is

99
00:07:00,507 --> 00:07:01,018
fourteen.

100
00:07:02,166 --> 00:07:06,946
With eight values, the median is the
average of the fourth and fifth, ten and

101
00:07:06,946 --> 00:07:08,374
eleven. Ten point five.

102
00:07:09,499 --> 00:07:14,432
The lower half is six, eight, eight, ten,
so Q one is eight. The upper half is

103
00:07:14,432 --> 00:07:18,353
eleven, twelve, fourteen, forty three, so
Q three is thirteen.

104
00:07:19,499 --> 00:07:22,081
The I Q R is thirteen minus eight, five.

105
00:07:23,199 --> 00:07:29,130
The upper fence is Q three plus one point
five times the I Q R: twenty point five.

106
00:07:30,266 --> 00:07:33,594
Forty three is above twenty point five, so
it's an outlier.

107
00:07:34,733 --> 00:07:39,934
The mean is fourteen, the median is ten
point five, and the I Q R is five. Forty

108
00:07:39,934 --> 00:07:44,226
three is an outlier, and it pulls the mean
above most of the data.

109
00:07:45,366 --> 00:07:51,022
Watch out. Always sort the data first.
Outliers pull the mean but barely move the

110
00:07:51,022 --> 00:07:55,841
median. So with outliers or skewed data,
report the median and I Q R.

111
00:07:56,966 --> 00:08:02,085
Your turn. For two, four, five, seven,
nine, find the mean and median. Then add

112
00:08:02,085 --> 00:08:05,649
thirty. Which changes more? Pause the
video and try it.

113
00:08:10,166 --> 00:08:15,895
The mean is five point four and the median
is five. Adding thirty makes the mean nine

114
00:08:15,895 --> 00:08:19,467
point five and the median six. The mean
changes more.

115
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:25,635
In this last lesson of Algebra One, we'll
display data so its shape is easy to see.

116
00:08:26,767 --> 00:08:30,479
A dot plot puts one dot above the number
line for each value.

117
00:08:30,929 --> 00:08:32,827
It works well for small data sets.

118
00:08:33,967 --> 00:08:39,104
A histogram groups values into equal-width
intervals, and draws a bar for how many

119
00:08:39,104 --> 00:08:39,919
fall in each.

120
00:08:40,369 --> 00:08:44,209
Its shape shows if the data is symmetric,
or skewed to one side.

121
00:08:45,333 --> 00:08:50,640
The five-number summary is the minimum,
first quartile, median, third quartile and

122
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:51,157
maximum.

123
00:08:51,607 --> 00:08:56,865
For one, three, four, six, seven, eight,
ten, eleven and fifteen, that's one, three

124
00:08:56,865 --> 00:08:59,842
and a half, seven, ten and a half, and
fifteen.

125
00:09:00,967 --> 00:09:03,121
A box plot draws those five numbers.

126
00:09:03,571 --> 00:09:08,554
The box runs from the first to the third
quartile, with a line at the median. The

127
00:09:08,554 --> 00:09:10,953
whiskers reach the minimum and maximum.

128
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:14,233
Box plots make comparisons easy.

129
00:09:14,683 --> 00:09:19,283
If one class's box sits higher and is
narrower, that class scored higher, and

130
00:09:19,283 --> 00:09:20,358
more consistently.

131
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:26,727
Your turn. In a box plot, the box runs
from twelve to twenty. What is the IQR?

132
00:09:27,177 --> 00:09:28,627
Pause the video and try it.

133
00:09:29,077 --> 00:09:30,656
Twenty minus twelve is eight.

134
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:35,320
Here's a worked example comparing two
groups with box plots.

135
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:41,573
Two classes have these five number
summaries. Class A: fifty five, seventy,

136
00:09:41,573 --> 00:09:46,621
seventy eight, eighty five, ninety five.
Class B: sixty two, seventy two, seventy

137
00:09:46,621 --> 00:09:51,169
six, eighty, eighty eight. Compare center
and spread. Which class is more

138
00:09:51,169 --> 00:09:51,855
consistent?

139
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:58,077
A box plot shows the minimum, Q one, the
median, Q three and the maximum.

140
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:03,509
The medians are seventy eight and seventy
six. Class A is slightly higher.

141
00:10:04,633 --> 00:10:10,091
The I Q Rs are eighty five minus seventy,
fifteen, and eighty minus seventy two,

142
00:10:10,091 --> 00:10:10,500
eight.

143
00:10:11,633 --> 00:10:13,831
The ranges are forty and twenty six.

144
00:10:14,967 --> 00:10:20,087
Class B has the smaller I Q R and range,
so its scores are more consistent.

145
00:10:21,233 --> 00:10:25,727
The centers are similar, with A slightly
higher, but class B is much more

146
00:10:25,727 --> 00:10:27,697
consistent, with half the I Q R.

147
00:10:28,833 --> 00:10:34,001
Watch out. When comparing, talk about both
center and spread. Each section of a box

148
00:10:34,001 --> 00:10:38,920
plot holds about a quarter of the data.
And a longer box means more spread, not

149
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:39,543
more data.

150
00:10:40,667 --> 00:10:45,563
Your turn. In class A, about what percent
of students scored above seventy? Pause

151
00:10:45,563 --> 00:10:46,832
the video and try it.

152
00:10:51,367 --> 00:10:55,356
Seventy is Q one, so about seventy five
percent scored above it.

153
00:10:56,500 --> 00:11:01,334
Let's finish Unit Ten and Algebra One with
a problem that uses radicals and a

154
00:11:01,334 --> 00:11:01,961
quadratic.

155
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:08,847
A square patio has an area of fifty square
meters, with a diagonal walkway across it.

156
00:11:08,847 --> 00:11:14,167
Find the side and the diagonal in simplest
radical form. Then, if edging costs four

157
00:11:14,167 --> 00:11:19,229
dollars a meter, how much does it cost to
edge all four sides and the diagonal?

158
00:11:20,367 --> 00:11:25,273
The area of a square is s squared, so s
squared is fifty and s is root fifty.

159
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:29,280
Root fifty simplifies to five root two
meters.

160
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:35,495
The diagonal makes a right triangle with
two sides, so d squared is fifty plus

161
00:11:35,495 --> 00:11:36,736
fifty, one hundred.

162
00:11:37,867 --> 00:11:39,573
The diagonal is ten meters.

163
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:46,097
The total edging is four sides plus the
diagonal: twenty root two plus ten meters.

164
00:11:47,233 --> 00:11:51,672
Twenty root two is about twenty eight
point two eight, so about thirty eight

165
00:11:51,672 --> 00:11:53,015
point two eight meters.

166
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:57,803
At four dollars a meter, that's about one
hundred fifty three dollars.

167
00:11:58,933 --> 00:12:04,122
The side is five root two meters, the
diagonal is exactly ten meters, and edging

168
00:12:04,122 --> 00:12:06,976
costs about one hundred fifty three
dollars.

169
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:13,616
Watch out. Keep exact radicals until the
very end. A square's diagonal is always

170
00:12:13,616 --> 00:12:17,615
the side times root two. And round only at
the final step.

171
00:12:18,733 --> 00:12:23,633
Your turn. A square has area eighteen
square centimeters. Find its side and

172
00:12:23,633 --> 00:12:26,051
diagonal. Pause the video and try it.

173
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:35,706
The side is root eighteen, which is three
root two. The diagonal is three root two

174
00:12:35,706 --> 00:12:38,259
times root two, which is six centimeters.

175
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:44,942
That completes this unit. Next up: Algebra
II, Unit 1. If this helped, subscribe to

176
00:12:44,942 --> 00:12:49,683
School STEM, Explained, and turn on
notifications so you don't miss it.

